`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The two-phase fetch's real payoff shows up in the log's `phase-2 diff` line: with a warm cache and zero changed MRs, the adapter never even builds the aliased discussions query — `changed=0` short-circuits straight past `enrichGQLMRsBatch`. That's why the 836ms warm run has no `phase-2 batch discussions done` log line at all, while the cold run's `changed=7` triggers one aliased request batching all 7 MRs' discussions in a single round trip (still far cheaper than 7 individual N+1 queries).

The `mrboard fetch` CLI command turned out to be a free cold-baseline probe purely as a side effect of its FetchOptions.Previous always being nil — no benchmark harness had to be written to satisfy the "measured, warm and cold" acceptance line.
